freezetest - a test for issue #1 (the freeze after changing DOpus's resolution)
==============================================================================

It does what you described, with plain screens instead of the programs:

  1. opens screen A (in place of Amelinium) in mode A and draws in it
  2. opens screen B (in place of DOpus) in mode A and draws in it
  3. changes B to mode B the way DOpus does: closes it, opens it again
  4. brings Workbench to the front
  5. brings screen A to the front, 6. Workbench again, 7. closes both

Each step is written to a log file and the file is closed again at once,
so if the Amiga freezes, the last line of the log names the step.

Set Workbench to the mode you use (1440x900, 24 bit) first, then in a Shell:

  freezetest A=7A00020A B=7A000008 LOG=SYS:freezetest.log

  7A00020A = 1440x900, 24 bit   (mode A, as your Workbench and Amelinium)
  7A000008 = 960x540, 8 bit     (mode B, as you switched DOpus to)

It pauses 5 seconds between steps (WAIT=2 for 2). After a freeze, reboot
and look at the end of SYS:freezetest.log (Type SYS:freezetest.log). When
it gets through, the last line is "PASS: no freeze".

Other modes: the number is 7A00 then the depth (00 = 8 bit, 01 = 16,
02 = 24, 03 = 32), then the size: 00 640x400, 01 640x480, 02 800x600,
03 1024x768, 04 1280x720, 05 1280x1024, 08 960x540, 09 1920x1080,
0A 1440x900. So 1920x1080 at 24 bit is 7A000209.

It reads and writes nothing else. GPL-3.0, part of PrismRTG.
